A data analyst collects, cleans, and interprets raw data to help organizations solve problems and make smart business decisions.
Coursera +1Key ResponsibilitiesData Collection & Cleaning: Gather data from databases, surveys, or web sources and remove errors or missing values.
Data Analysis: Run statistical methods and queries to spot trends, track key performance indicators (KPIs), and find patterns.Data Visualization: 
Build charts, graphs, and interactive dashboards to present findings clearly.Business Recommendations: 
Turn numbers into clear stories and actionable advice for company leaders. 
